{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And you shall say: I will eat meat.</b> The Torah teaches a rule of proper conduct (derekh eretz): a person should not eat meat except out of abundance and expansion, and this is the sense of כי ירחיב — 'when He enlarges.'" "<b>You may eat meat, according to the desire of your soul.</b> He permitted them unconsecrated meat (בשר חולין) when they would enter the Land, because in the wilderness all the meat that they ate was entirely of shelamim offerings."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:54.359144798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}